    "name": "loss_logsigmoid_squared_advantage_gap_clipped_normalized_v2",
    "intuition": "Fixed potential high similarity by introducing adaptive margin scaled by the absolute advantage_gap instead of squared, and incorporating a soft margin clipping with tanh to smoothly limit margin influence. Also normalized loss by weighted sum of absolute advantage_gap plus epsilon to maintain scale invariance and stable gradients, enhancing preference sensitivity while preventing extreme margin penalties.",
    "pseudocode": "adv_abs = abs(advantage_gap)\nadaptive_margin = margin * adv_abs\nclipped_margin = 0.5 * (ops.tanh(adaptive_margin) + 1.0) * adaptive_margin  # smooth clipping\nx = clamp(alpha * scale * (log_prob_w - log_prob_l) - clipped_margin, -20, 20)\nraw_loss = -logsigmoid(x)\nloss = sum(weight * raw_loss) / (sum(weight * adv_abs) + epsilon)",
